Run the demo
  You launch exactly THREE things by hand. Everything else is a workflow node -
  the individual job templates will fail if launched on their own, because they
  read artifacts from the nodes before them.

  1. JOB TEMPLATE  "{{ jt_break_apache }}"
     Automation Execution > Templates. Breaks Apache on the target.

  2. Watch Automation Decisions > Rulebook Activations pick up the Kafka event.
     "{{ enrichment_workflow_name }}"
     then runs AUTOMATICALLY - you do not launch it.
     Check Mattermost #{{ mattermost_channel }} for the logs and the AI RCA.

  3. WORKFLOW       "{{ remediation_workflow_name }}"
     Same Templates list; its Type column says "Workflow job template".
     Launch it, and the survey shows two boxes: a known-good prompt on the
     required field, and the prompt Red Hat AI wrote in the reference field.
     Copy the AI one over if you are happy with it - that review IS the demo -
     then Next > Finish.
     The generated playbook is committed to
     {{ gitea_url_external }}/{{ gitea_admin_user }}/{{ demo_playbook_repo }}

  4. JOB TEMPLATE  "{{ jt_execute_remediation }}"
     Launch with Limit = {{ demo_target_hostname }}. Applies the AI's fix.

  5. Confirm http://{{ target_public_ip }} is serving again.

Reset between runs
  Launch job template "{{ jt_restore_apache }}".

Do NOT launch these directly - they are workflow nodes and need their inputs:
